Hi.

I ascended a Convict in UnNetHack (latest trunk version). It didn't go 
very smoothly but I still ascended the first Convict I tried.

I would post a dumplog but one didn't get generated and I can't be 
bothered to extract the infomation from the ttyrecs.

This particular game was particularly challenging, not only because of 
the Convict role but because RNG didn't seem to want me to win and 
refused to give me essential items. I won anyway.


Now. I didn't know how the Convict plays before I started the game. 
Suffice to say I was a little surprised to start with only an iron ball, 
some rocks, a shirt and a rat pet. Very soon I also noticed I was hungry 
very early, before prayer can be done. I wielded the iron ball for weapon 
and it worked well.

At this point I was told by the friendly chatters in the UnNetHack IRC 
channel that the Convict also starts with small negative luck penalty and 
negative alignment. Uh-oh.

Going down the stairs is a gamble with the iron ball. Luckily I survived. 
At turn 250 or so I was already fainting and couldn't find any corpses or 
food items to eat. Tried prayer and it succeeded! Starvation averted for 
now.

I saw a ring and a scroll shop on levels 2 and 3, didn't let me in 
because I looked like an escaped criminal. Assholes.

I went to the mines, got into a tight spot with giant ants and orcs with 
wands of magic missiles but managed to barely survive. Elbereth was with 
me.

At minetown the guardsfolk weren't exactly welcoming. I killed a few 
watchmen with the iron ball (it's a very good iron ball) but I did not 
dare to face off with a watch captain just yet. I grabbed some leather 
gloves off a dead watchman and backpedaled to the Dungeons of Doom.

What followed was a trip to the Sokoban. I was still using the iron ball 
as a weapon because it is excellent at reducing the hp of enemies and 
hadn't yet come across a better weapon.

At the first sokoban level a Woodland-elf zapped me with a wand of 
lightning. From full hp to 8 hp. I had two choices I could make: pray or 
hit. I thought prayer probably wouldn't really save me so I hit. That was 
the correct choice.

The third and last Sokoban level (UnNetHack only has 3 levels) I was 
meeted with a level I hadn't ever seen before. I think I had to squeeze 
three times in total but the time I spent there cancelled the luck 
penalties out. I think.

I chose the cloak of magic resistance as the prize over amulet of 
reflection and a bag of holding. The cloak was +4. Nice.

And just a little later a nymph stole it (along with my trusted iron 
ball). And totally disappeared. Just nowhere. I gave up and went back to 
mines.

Nothing interesting happened for a while. I got the luckstone.

Using a potion of object detection on the level where the nymph stole the 
MR cloak I noticed it was in a vault. That bitch. Using the dwarvish 
mattock I kindly borrowed from a dwarf in the mines I dug in and made her 
dead.

At this time my AC was -3 with the cloak and had 113 maximum hp. The 
mattock is also a very powerful weapon (as a non-artifact) so I was in 
good shape. My turn count was about 16k which is quite a lot at this 
stage of game (my average is about 25k for a normal game, I think).

I found the quest portal and took a peek to see what kind of quest the 
Convict would have. I found this guy who apparently has a problem with a 
some warden lady. I got accepted to the quest but decided not to go yet 
as I had no idea how tough the Warden would be or if there would be any 
tricks in the quest. 

There was a chaotic altar on the quest home level. Convenient! I prayed 
for some holy water.

Going deeper in the dungeon I got to the Medusa level. I had no way to 
cross water so I just dug down (I had an instrument for castle and MR so 
thought I might be ready). I walked stairs up right away and killed 
Medusa. Perseus had a shield of reflection but I couldn't use it with the 
mattock. I picked it up anyway because I thought it'll be useful to 
defend myself against dragons in the castle.


Not everything goes well. I got the castle variant that will not let me 
reach the wand of wishing unless I have some means of levitation, jumping 
or plugging holes. I had none of those. I also couldn't go back because I 
can't cross medusa. I didn't have any cursed teleportation scrolls. What 
do I do? Why, dig down to the Valley of the Dead of course!

I worked my way to Gehennom. Very soon, I met a chromatic dragon. Not the 
quest nemesis but a new dragon type in UnNetHack. I killed it and it 
dropped chromatic dragon scales. Those scales give every resistance. At 
least every relevant one. It also has only 1 AC. I started wearing it for 
the reflection. This also meant dumping the elven mithril coat I was 
wearing and now I had 4 AC in Gehennom.

I almost got my ass handed over to me on the Asmodeus level. In 
UnNetHack, the demon princes don't respect Elbereth. Normally Asmodeus 
isn't dangerous (his ice attack is easily nullified by having cold 
resistance) but I had practically no armor that protects me against 
physical damage. I did manage to run for the downstairs to heal. Then I 
lured Asmodeus there and killed him. He zapping his wands saved me some 
time because they had no effect (as opposed to him using melee attacks 
that would have hurt me).

A little later I met Juiblex who would have killed me because I didn't 
have a unicorn horn but it appears Convict has illness resistance! 
Juiblex didn't last long against a high quality thoroughly rusty 
thoroughly corroded dwarven mattock.

I found Vlad stairs and got myself the amulet of life saving and water 
walking boots. I also found a ring of levitation. Now I had the items to 
do castle! Also, for the first time, I didn't go to Vlad because I 
thought I might not win against him. And that's pathetic.

I used a cursed scroll of teleportation to go back (I found it at some 
point). Walking back wouldn't work because I would have to fight Orcus 
and it would be unlikely I would win with my weak character. The scroll 
brought me up high enough to walk out.

I went to the castle and levitated over the trap doors, grabbed the wand 
and wished for a bag of holding.

Then I walked back to the Dungeons of Doom to my pile of scrolls and 
potions I had dropped next to stairs. I enchanted my mattock and some of 
my armor and got from 4 AC to -8 AC. I was about to do the quest.

I was a little nervous because I still had no idea how tough the warden 
would be. If she would be as tough as Master Kaen I would be killed 
pretty quickly, barring the wand of sleeping I could use.

The quest levels weren't anything really special. Some long zig-zag 
levels and prison guards. The prison guards ask me 9000 zorkmids to avoid 
arrest. Are you kidding me? A mattock to the head is what I give you!

The warden was a disappointment. She was a pushover. She didn't even 
start with the quest artifact in her inventory (she had to go and get it).

I got the Iron Ball of Even More Disappointment. I spoiled myself on what 
it does and in UnNetHack it gives MR, displacement, searching and 
warning. And invocation as a digging wand. I already had MR and the other 
bonuses aren't enough to justify lugging that heavy thing around (unlike 
Valkyries' Orb of Fate, that one is awesome). It might have worked as a 
weapon (depends if it's better than a regular iron ball). I left the ball 
on the level.

I visited the Black Market. Nothing very interesting happened there, I 
bought gauntlets of dexterity and a scroll. If I had more resources, I 
might have attempted to kill the One-Eyed Sam or make a run for heaps of 
loot.

Went back to Gehennom. Killed Baalzebub, Orcus and Vlad. Also found the 
vibrating square. My character still had -8 AC and turn count was 35k at 
this point. My maximum hp was 152 and I was at experience level 19.

At this point I noticed I don't have the Bell of Opening in my inventory. 
Did I forget to pick it up? I teleported back to the Dungeon and ran to 
the quest end level. Nope. The bell is not anywhere. I tried magic 
mapping on the level to see if it's somewhere hidden in the same way as 
the quest artifact wasn't at Warden's foot at start. But no. It wasn't 
anywhere.

I took the ttyrec I was recording and searched if I had seen it. Nope.

Then I went to the source code. I noticed the bell is not generated at 
all. The Convict is unwinnable.

What do I do? I didn't want to stop since I had worked on the character 
hard and had to overcome many tough situations. So I modified the source 
code to make bells of opening wishable from magic lamps and wished for 
one.

And here I made a little mistake. I used discovery mode to wish for the 
item in case I made a mistake and had to roll back. I accidentally made 
my save to be in discovery mode. Oh well. I promised myself I'll press Y 
if I happen to die.

I got the bell now so now I can go back to Gehennom and start the 
ascension run.

I had surplus wands of death and with the CDSM I can safely walk with 
wielded cockatrice corpses (and even eat them if I want). Rodney wouldn't 
be a problem for a while. I also had a (1:1) wand of wishing (the only 
wish apart from the bell was the bag of holding I wished at castle). My 
character was weak in the AC department although it now had -12 AC. Turn 
count was closing in to 40k (an unusually slow game for me but happens 
sometimes in unlucky games such as this).

At the Sanctum, Cthulhu proceeded to drink a cursed potion of gain level 
right at start.

At the level above, Cthulhu killed me. Luckily I had an amulet of life 
saving. I zapped him with death and started looking for the amulet he 
dropped (in UnNetHack, if the amulet is dropped, it teleports to a short 
distance). I couldn't find the amulet though. I decided I would go to the 
level above to heal and then come back to the level.

Cthulhu didn't revive for some reason. He just disappeared. I looked for 
the amulet but still couldn't find it.

Finally, Rodney showed up and kindly fetched it for me from somewhere. As 
a reward I sent him to heaven. Actually I think he probably went to hell 
instead. But it's not like he can't come back.

Nothing particularly interesting happened while I was working my way up.

On the planes I was tortured by RNG. On the Plane of Earth, I explored 
every pocket on the level (there are 10 in total). The portal just didn't 
seem to be anywhere. It took 1000 turns to finally find the portal in one 
of the pockets that I thought had already explored properly.

I think I spent so much time on the Plane of Earth, the Plane of Air had 
an unusually large amount of monsters on entrance. I put on conflict and 
levitation and started searching for the portal.

It also took a while to find the portal on this level; I had to go over 
left and right of the level a few times. In UnNetHack the portal can also 
be on the same side as where you begin the level.

Then I got on the Plane of Water. That was mostly boring and not 
dangerous.

Plane of Fire was the real deal. What a cruel game. It took forever to 
find the portal and I killed 7 Archons on the level (by hitting them a 
lot with a dwarvish mattock). I got summon stormed a few times but got 
out by playing my favorite songs using the tooled horn.

Finally when I was starting to seriously get pissed off, I searched the 
ttyrec for any messages if the Amulet of Yendor was warm at some point (I 
was wielding it most of the time) and lucky for me, there was such a 
point! However, I still couldn't find the portal quickly and I think I 
finished off two more Archons while trying to find it.

Then I wrested the wishing wand for a blessed magic marker, wrote blessed 
charging scrolls, charged the bell of opening and some death wands and 
ringed the bell at the place where the amulet was warm. Found the portal! 
RNG, you are going to pay for this bullshit you put me through.

Astral was uneventful; the correct altar was the middle one I found as 
the second high altar.


----------------------------------------------------------------------
I ascended at turn 43133, with 171 hpmax, at experience level 19, with 
-11 AC, wielding a +5 blessed rustproof dwarvish mattock, wearing an 
amulet of life saving and conflict. The only conducts that were held were 
artiwishless and polyselfless. I got 1325576 points.
----------------------------------------------------------------------





The Convict patch needs work on the quest. Apart from the obvious Bell of 
Opening issue and I think it could use more variety in the quest (many of 
the monsters either have irrelevant behaviour (like bribing behaviour) or 
just seem too generic).

Also I believe the (intentional?) combination of hunger, luck and 
alignment penalty is unnecessary and makes the earliest game too much 
about luck. I have nothing against difficulty as long as it's...tasteful 
kind of difficulty.

Other than that I think the Convict patch is a great idea as I've longed 
for a "hard mode" that didn't involve voluntarily tying my hands back 
like playing conducts.

